 # Changelog
 
+## 0.5.1 (unreleased)
+
+Additive only (issues #703, #711); every default is unchanged. Nothing here was compiled or run for this entry.
+
+- **Linux: `SandboxPolicy::system_roots(SystemRoots)`** (#703). `SystemRoots::Default` (the default) keeps the
+  implicit read and execute roots `/usr /bin /sbin /lib /lib64 /etc /proc /dev /sys`. `SystemRoots::Minimal(vec)`
+  grants only the listed absolute roots (validated absolute and NUL-free) and `SystemRoots::None` grants none, so a
+  tier can leave `/proc` (the `environ` of same-user processes), `/etc` and `/sys` out of the Landlock ruleset. A
+  non-empty `Minimal` counts as a listed path for `LandlockMode::SkipWhenNoPaths`. Ignored on macOS and Windows.
+- **macOS Strict profile: three opt-in tightenings** (#711), all off by default so existing profiles are unchanged
+  (a PTY child still needs its tty): `SandboxPolicy::deny_tty(true)` drops the `/dev/tty` and `/dev/ttys*`
+  read, write and ioctl grant and denies terminal devices (also removes the `^/dev/tty` write from `WriteOnly`);
+  `scope_metadata(true)` replaces the global `(allow file-read-metadata)` with literal rules for the root `/`
+  walk (every ancestor of each granted and system root); `minimal_system_reads(true)` drops `/Applications`,
+  `/etc` and `/private/etc` from the always-readable and executable system locations. **Not verified on a Mac.**
+- Not done: #562 tokio `AsyncWrite`/`AsyncRead` wrappers (`ConfinedPipedChild`) still need an optional `tokio`
+  dependency; see the 0.5.0 entry.
+
